---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const steps = [
  'load a byte from [R0]',
  'load a byte from [R1]',
  'compare them',
  'advance R0 and R1, decrement R2',
  'stop if they differ or R2 is zero',
];

const rules = [
  { name: 'Length', text: 'Instructions are 1 to 18 bytes long. The first one or two bytes give the length, so the decoder knows where the next instruction starts before it looks at any operand.' },
  { name: 'Commit', text: 'An instruction becomes visible all at once, however many internal steps it takes. A repeated instruction does this once per iteration.' },
  { name: 'Interrupted work', text: 'Repeated instructions and vector gather/scatter can stop partway. Their progress is in their own operands, such as the counter and pointers in the memcmp example, so running the same instruction again finishes the rest.' },
  { name: 'Implementations', text: 'A small core can run the internal steps one at a time. A wide core can run independent steps in parallel. Both implement the same instruction.' },
];

const history = [
  { when: 'May 2026', text: 'First commit. Compound instructions were already split into internal steps, but the rest looked like a cleaned-up CISC: separate data and address registers, modifier prefixes, and hidden state for resuming repeated instructions.' },
  { when: 'July 2026', text: 'The encoding was redone so every instruction states its own length. The register file became R0 to R15, and interrupts and exceptions moved to one event model.' },
  { when: 'August 2026', text: 'The decoder started being generated from the specification, including a SystemVerilog version. The hidden resume state was removed; an interrupted repeat now restarts by decoding its prefix again.' },
];
---

<Base title="Why Bedrock" description="Bedrock's design philosophy: encode intent, decompose execution.">
  <section class="wrap hero">
    <p class="kicker">Why Bedrock</p>
    <h1>Encode intent.<br />Decompose execution.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A Bedrock instruction can carry a whole loop. The processor splits it into internal steps using a fixed
      template for that instruction, instead of rebuilding the loop from many small instructions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap block">
    <h2 class="block-title"><i>01</i>memcmp in one instruction</h2>
    <div class="example">
      <div>
        <p class="c">memcmp(a, b, n)</p>
        <pre><code>REPEQ R2, CMP.B [R0++], [R1++]</code></pre>
      </div>
      <ol>{steps.map((step) => <li>{step}</li>)}</ol>
    </div>
    <p class="body">
      This is all of <code>memcmp</code>: one instruction, with R0 and R1 pointing at the two buffers and R2 holding the
      length. The pointers advance through the <code>[R0++]</code> addressing form, so there is no separate increment,
      compare, or branch. Each iteration commits on its own, and if an interrupt arrives partway through, R0, R1 and R2
      already hold the progress. Returning to the same instruction continues from there.
    </p>
    <p class="body">
      The project calls this style DISC, for decomposition-oriented instruction set computer. The core receives the
      whole loop as one instruction and splits each iteration into the listed steps from a fixed template.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap block">
    <h2 class="block-title"><i>02</i>Rules that follow from it</h2>
    <dl class="rules">
      {rules.map((r) => (
        <div>
          <dt>{r.name}</dt>
          <dd>{r.text}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap block">
    <h2 class="block-title"><i>03</i>History</h2>
    <ol class="timeline">
      {history.map((h) => (
        <li>
          <span class="date">{h.when}</span>
          <p>{h.text}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p class="body">
      The rules in the previous section describe the design as it stood after these changes. The longer rationale is
      in <a href="https://github.com/bedrock-proj/spec/issues/4">spec#4</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    margin-top: 56px;
  }
  .kicker {
    font: 500 12px var(--mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  h1 {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font: 600 clamp(36px, 7vw, 60px) / 1.05 var(--sans);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }
  .lede {
    max-width: 660px;
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-size: 18px;
  }



  .example {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .example .c {
    font: 400 13px var(--mono);
    color: var(--mute);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .example pre {
    font: 500 19px var(--mono);
    white-space: pre-wrap;
  }
  .example ol {
    font: 400 13px/1.9 var(--mono);
    color: var(--mute);
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .body {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .rules {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0 32px;
  }
  .rules div {
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--faint);
  }
  .rules dt {
    font: 600 13px var(--mono);
  }
  .rules dd {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--mute);
  }
  .timeline {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--faint);
    margin-left: 6px;
  }
  .timeline li {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 110px 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 0 0 22px 22px;
  }
  .timeline li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -7px;
    top: 5px;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 2px solid var(--accent);
  }
  .date {
    font: 400 12px/22px var(--mono);
    color: var(--mute);
  }
  .timeline p {
    font-size: 15px;
  }



  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .example {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      padding: 16px;
    }
    .example pre {
      font-size: 15px;
    }
    .rules {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .timeline li {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
